    <h1 class="content-page__title">Support</h1>
    <p class="content-page__intro">Find answers to common questions and get help with Open Phonics.</p>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">How long does the program take?</h3>
      <p>At one lesson per day, the 150-lesson program takes about 5-6 months. Each lesson is 5-10 minutes. Some learners may go faster; others may need to repeat lessons.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">What age is this for?</h3>
      <p>Open Phonics works for any beginning reader, typically ages 4-8. It can also be used for older learners or adults who need systematic phonics instruction.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Do I need teaching experience?</h3>
      <p>No. Every lesson has a complete script telling you exactly what to say and do. Read the <a href="/guide/">Guide</a> before starting.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">What if the learner is struggling?</h3>
      <p>Repeat the lesson the next day. Do not move forward until the learner can complete the lesson with confidence. It is normal to repeat lessons 2-3 times. If the learner is still struggling after several repetitions, go back a few lessons and rebuild from there.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Can I skip lessons?</h3>
      <p>No. The lessons are carefully sequenced. Each lesson builds on the previous one. Skipping ahead will leave gaps in the learner's knowledge.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Does it work offline?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Open Phonics is a Progressive Web App (PWA). After your first visit, it works without an internet connection.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">How do I save progress?</h3>
      <p>Progress is saved automatically in your browser. You can create multiple student profiles on the Lessons page. Use the Export button to download a backup file, and the Import button to restore it on another device.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Is my data private?</h3>
      <p>Yes. All data stays on your device. We do not collect, store, or transmit any personal information. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Troubleshooting</h2>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">The pointer dot is not moving</h3>
      <p>Make sure JavaScript is enabled in your browser. Try refreshing the page. If the issue persists, try a different browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, or Safari).</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Progress was lost</h3>
      <p>Progress is stored in your browser's localStorage. Clearing your browser data, using private/incognito mode, or switching browsers will reset progress. Use the Export button regularly to back up your data.</p>

      <h3 style="font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:var(--space-lg);margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)">Dark mode is not working</h3>
      <p>Click the sun/moon icon in the top right corner of the header to toggle dark mode. If it does not respond, try refreshing the page.</p>
    </section>

